      {
        "id": "comment-title",
        "type": "comment",
        "position": {
          "x": 0.0,
          "y": -200.0
        },
        "data": {
          "text": "## Output multiplier α: rich ↔ lazy regime\n\n**Paper:** Chizat, Oyallon & Bach — *On Lazy Training in Differentiable Programming* (arXiv:1812.07956)  \n**Reproduced as:** Figure 2 of review paper arXiv:2604.21691\n\n**Setup:** Shallow ReLU network `f(x) = α · Σᵢ aᵢ ReLU(wᵢᵀx)` on 2-D synthetic teacher data (3 teacher neurons).\n\n**Claim to verify:**\n- Small α → **rich / feature-learning** regime: hidden neurons migrate toward teacher directions; good test generalisation.\n- Large α → **lazy / NTK** regime: weights barely move from init; model behaves as a linearisation; performance plateaus at random-feature level.\n\n**Sweep:** `outputScale α ∈ [0.01, 0.05, 0.1, 0.5, 1.0, 2.0, 5.0]` (multi-value field on student MLP — one training run per value).\n\n**Key plots:**\n1. Test loss vs training step for each α (training_visualization — run each α separately or use train series).\n2. Hidden neuron weight vectors wᵢ ∈ ℝ² in the 2-D input plane at convergence (model_weight_tensors → slice first linear layer → tensor_viz_scatter; see comment node at right).\n3. Weight displacement vs step per α (observable_weight_displacement).\n\n**Notes:**\n- Output layer init: aᵢ ~ N(0,1/n) then ×α via `outputScale`. Do NOT re-scale after init.\n- Use n ≥ 100 neurons; transition is invisible for small n.\n- SGD with lr=0.01, no momentum, full-batch (batchSize=-1).",
          "instanceTitle": "Experiment overview",
          "comment": "\n\n---\n**协议说明**:本 template 保留 PR #18 的展示风格参数(α=0.01、τ=0.01、lr=0.01、lossScale=1、无 warmup),适合交互探索轨迹迁移。机器可查的现象证据用的是干净受控协议(α∈{0.1,1} 对比、τ=1.0、lossScale=1/α² 时标补偿、lr warmup)——见 scripts/phenomena/rich_vs_lazy.py;两者不是同一实验协议。"
        },
        "parentId": null,
        "extent": null,
        "hidden": null,
        "style": null
      },
