        "data": {
          "text": "## 2D weight scatter (post-training)\n\nTo reproduce Fig 2 scatter plots (neuron weight vectors in input space):\n\n1. Connect `model_weight_tensors → tensor_list` to a `tensor_selector` and pick layer `0.weight` (shape [width, 2]).\n2. Slice column 0 (x-coords) and column 1 (y-coords) via two `tensor_slicing` nodes.\n3. Feed both slices into `tensor_viz_scatter` (tensor_1 = x-dim, tensor_2 = y-dim).\n\nRich regime (small α): neuron directions cluster near the 3 teacher neuron directions.\nLazy regime (large α): directions spread uniformly over the 2D input sphere.",
          "instanceTitle": "Scatter viz instructions"
        },
        "parentId": null,
